# Ocean Nomad agent

- On a new machine read docs/RESTORE_ON_NEW_PC.md and docs/AGENT_HANDOFF.md. Archived prompts do not authorize runtime actions.
- Follow the latest requested stage; a roadmap request does not start another gameplay run.
- Reuse the saved UI, navigation, interaction and combat modules. Current scoped approvals and remaining gaps are in owning cards and docs/AGENT_HANDOFF.md. The five prepared missions form the current onboarding group; hands_collect is deferred. Metadata lookup is implemented; semantic retrieval is not.
- Use brain/ROADMAP.md for implementation order and brain/CONTEXT_POLICY.md for retrieval.
- Retrieve only the current task, local region, active skill and linked failure constraints.
- Do not preload all knowledge, chats, source files or scene objects on every action.
- Proposed brain interfaces are not installed MCP tools. Until implemented, read narrowly selected files explicitly.
- Separate requirements, source-derived claims, runtime observations and hypotheses.
- A dispatched action is not proof of success. Check postconditions and preserve failures.
- Keep ordinary gameplay input separate from teleportation, item grants and quest-state changes used for fixture setup.
- Keep private game sources, credentials, local SQLite stores and raw runs out of Git.
- One executor controls a Unity instance at a time.
